  "_help": "Material 3 baseline (source #6750A4), light. The values are the M3 token set (material-web tokens/versions/latest). gohud's required keys are M3 roles: background = surface, surface = surface-container-high (the dialog), text = on-surface, secondary and muted = on-surface-variant, border = outline, accent = primary, danger = error, track = secondary-container. Two keys differ from the M3 card because gohud keeps panel, card and raised cell 1.12:1 apart (tools/check_contrast.py): surface_soft = surface-dim, surface_high = outline-variant. success, warning and info are M3 custom colors (harmonized with the source, tone 40). Every M3 colour role is also an md_* key of the same name for app code (the ones above repeated as md_primary, md_on_surface and so on): GoUi.color(&\"md_secondary_container\"). Change colors here, then run python3 tools/make_theme.py material_light.",
